      en: "Former City Hall in Santiago, historic site of governance. Seat of government. Colonial period. Historic building. City administration. Thus, the site is among the characteristic points of Cuba, the Caribbean island nation, reflecting the interplay of history, tobacco and sugarcane cultivation, and tropical nature. Located in Cuba, the largest island state in the Caribbean. Tropical-humid climate with distinct wet and dry seasons. Havana, the capital, is the country's political and cultural hub. The region is closely tied to tobacco, sugarcane and coffee cultivation."
